+
+def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
+    """
+    Draw a turning path in the right panel according to the left-program stripes.
+
+    Input structure:
+    - The grid is split by a vertical full-height divider into a left panel, divider, right panel.
+    - The left panel is filled with full-height vertical stripes; each stripe color is red, cyan/teal, or yellow.
+    - The stripe thickness equals how many steps to walk, and each stripe color controls turning.
+    - The right panel is black except for one green start pixel on its boundary.
+
+    Rule:
+    - Read stripe colors from left to right in the left panel; each stripe yields one instruction: color as turn and width as step count.
+    - Start at the green boundary pixel in the right panel, initially pointing from the boundary toward panel interior.
+    - For each instruction: rotate by color (red=right turn, cyan/teal=left turn, yellow=straight), then move exactly the stripe thickness steps, painting every visited cell green.
+    - The right panel has no overlaps in valid inputs and may be shorter than the full grid.
